# Cloudflare Pages headers for AI Déjà Vu.
#
# The compiled modules in /dist are the whole problem: Pages defaults them to
# max-age=14400, so a browser can import a four-hour-old build after a deploy.
# That produced a missing extractor option and, once, a dead page from a stale
# IndexedDB version constant. Revalidating them costs one conditional request
# and removes the entire class of bug.
#
# sw.js must never be cached at all: if an old sw.js is served, the old BUILD id
# stays live, the cache name never changes, and nothing ever busts.

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/dist/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
